  "details": "TL;DR: Index finger curle is too aggressive when simple capacitive contact is made with the trigger.\n\nSo previous to the VRChat IK 2.0 update, when I contacted my finger on the index trigger (only capacitive contact) it would only move my VR finger a few cm, and as I depresesd the index trigger (mechanical movement of the trigger) it would smoothly close my VR finger into a fist. But since the update, when only making capacitive contact with the trigger, my VR finger will curle aggressively and jump to almost totally closed, basically I lose all that fine motor movement that I could control before. It's very jarring and immersion breaking and not the way it functioned previous to the update. And turning on or off the legacy fingers makes no difference.\n\nI don't have any video of how it worked before, but I've made a video of how it's working now: https://youtu.be/oaDvZURCgNo\n\nThe middle finger trigger still works as intended, moving all the other 3 fingers smoothly from open to closed. \n\nMy setup: Virtual desktop, with Valve Index Controller emulation enabled. Hardware is Quest Pro and Quest 3 controllers.\n\nAnyone else experience this?\n\nThank you <3",
